Allow yourself to get crowned and the minimum increase in
prayer timeout does make it too unlikely.  Avoid getting
crowned and the possible range of prayer timeout values
stays so small a few tiny sacs is enough.

> Does anyone have some guesstimate of a sucessfull prayer to unwanted
> luckboost ratio? I'm trying to figure out if this is worthwile to me.

If you are trying to restock your library you are doing *many*
cycles of sac/reconcile/pray.  Note that the game tries to give
you unknown spellbooks each time (I think it tries XP times
for the random number generator to make one in one of your
schools that you don't already know and only gives you a
random one if those attempts fail).  That means you will need
a LOT of books before you have the ones you need.

Even if the ratio is a dozen books per unwanted luck boost,
you will want enough books that it becomes extremely likely
to get an unwanted luck boost.

My experience of trying this is coaligned unicorns never seem
to run out on the level I'm using.  I don't know what that says
about the odds of it happening, but any character without the
"create monster" spell rarely is able to pull off the
sac/reconcile/pray cycle for books unless they have a lot of
of ways to create monsters.  A tourist with a bag of tricks and
the card should be able to do it in cycles while the card
goes from ignoring you to granting charging again.  If you are
not willing to kill coaligned unicorns for the needed luck
decrease it likely will not be worth staying in the cycle.

Each time I have tried the cycle I have eventually lost track
of my exact luck count and ended up crowned.  At least
with a wizard I've managed to stay in the loop long enough
to get a +FoD to carry so the crowning yielded Stormy.  That
means I have a ton of books before I lost track and got crowned.



